  "scope": "Prove even and odd factors distinct by remainders",
  "validation": "A current-source ArithmeticBinomFactorial provider was rebuilt; paired target and sole tracked direct Lean client ArithmeticHalfBinomial builds pass with identical client objects. Eight exact-target-object-pinned probes report equal target declarations, type/axioms, and sampled default simp and instance registrations. Target source-current BinaryPopulation and Factorial's direct Pascal input match prior successful producer receipts. Two existing linter warnings disappear while one remains.",
  "limitations": [
    "Direct client providers ArithmeticHalfBinomialSandwich and ArithmeticBinomExpansion have no source/object producer match in the documented local records search; no staleness conclusion follows. Wider transitive closure remains cached and downstream clients were not rebuilt.",
    "Declaration, type/axiom and sampled registration equality does not establish proof-body identity or equality of all persistent Lean extensions.",
    "Compiled objects excluded. Recorded build and probe paths refer to temporary directories; full replay requires external object dependencies and environment. Intermediate long proof and its overwritten records are exploratory only, as README states."
  ],
